WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.080
Without Notch, a fly embryo builds too much nervous system and too little skin.

2
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.020
Notch is what lets a cell be told, not you.

3
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.920
But the message never leaves the cell that makes it.

4
00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:18.800
The ligand is a protein fixed in that cell's membrane, and the receptor is fixed in

5
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.280
its neighbour's. The two usually meet where cells touch.

6
00:00:23.183 --> 00:00:24.703
Binding is not enough.

7
00:00:25.303 --> 00:00:29.883
Just outside the membrane, Notch is folded into a lock that hides the spot where it

8
00:00:29.883 --> 00:00:33.543
can be cut. In the standard account, the receptor must be pulled.

9
00:00:34.103 --> 00:00:38.883
The sending cell draws its ligand back inside, and the tug passes to the receptor it

10
00:00:38.883 --> 00:00:41.443
holds. The pull peels the lock open.

11
00:00:42.217 --> 00:00:47.397
In mammalian cells, the first cut comes while the receptor is made, and it carries

12
00:00:47.397 --> 00:00:53.057
no signal. After the pull, an atom protease makes the second cut, just outside the

13
00:00:53.057 --> 00:00:58.457
membrane. The outer part leaves with the ligand, and a stub stays in the membrane.

14
00:00:59.137 --> 00:01:02.997
Then gamma γ-secretase makes the third cut, inside the membrane.

15
00:01:03.517 --> 00:01:08.697
It accepts a membrane protein only after most of the outer part is gone, so the

16
00:01:08.697 --> 00:01:09.997
second cut comes first.

17
00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:15.790
That cut frees the inner part of the receptor, which is called NICD.

18
00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:21.770
It enters the nucleus, where CSL binds target genes only briefly until signal

19
00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:26.970
arrives. In the standard account, CSL keeps those genes off with co -repressors.

20
00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:33.190
NICD binds CSL, displaces the co -repressors, and recruits a co -activator called

21
00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:35.290
Mastermind. The genes turn on.

22
00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:41.530
In a kinase cascade, each active enzyme modifies many substrates, so the signal

23
00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:42.710
grows at every step.

24
00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.650
Notch has no second messenger and no kinase relay.

25
00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:50.190
Between the membrane and the gene, nothing multiplies.

26
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:53.090
One cut receptor gives one inner part.

27
00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.950
A cut cannot be undone, so each receptor signals once.

28
00:01:57.833 --> 00:02:00.113
What this design buys the cell is a count.

29
00:02:00.693 --> 00:02:05.073
The amount of inner part made follows, one for one, the number of receptors a

30
00:02:05.073 --> 00:02:06.453
neighbour has pulled and cut.

31
00:02:06.973 --> 00:02:09.893
A cell mostly hears Notch from the cells it touches.

32
00:02:10.613 --> 00:02:16.093
Keep this rule: one receptor, pulled and cut, gives one inner part and one message.
